## DESCRIPTION
## Calculus Two, Sequences
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject(Calculus - single variable)
## DBchapter(Infinite sequences and series)
## DBsection(Limit of a sequence)
## Date(09/16/2018)
## Institution(Community College of Denver, Colorado Community College System)
## Author(Brittni Lorton)
## KEYWORDS('calculus', 'sequences', 'limit of a sequence')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros("PGstandard.pl", "PGML.pl", "PGcourse.pl",);

Context('Numeric')->variables->are(n => "Real");

$a = random(2, 5);

BEGIN_PGML

Find the limit of the sequence [``\{a_n\} = \{([$a]n)^{1/n}-n^{1/n}\}``].

[``\lim_{n \to \infty} a_n=``][_]{Real(0)}{5} 
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
First, let's find for any [`c>1`],
[``` 
\begin{aligned}
\lim_{n \to \infty} c^{1/n} & = \lim_{n \to \infty}  e^{\ln c^{1/n}} \\
& = e^{\lim_{n \to \infty} \frac{\ln c}{n}} = e^0 = 1
\end{aligned}
```]
and 
[``` 
\begin{aligned}
\lim_{n \to \infty} n^{1/n} & = \lim_{n \to \infty}  e^{\ln n^{1/n}} \\
& = e^{\lim_{n \to \infty} \frac{\ln n}{n}} = e^0 = 1
\end{aligned}
```]

[```\begin{aligned}
\lim_{n \to \infty} a_n & = \lim_{n \to \infty} \left(([$a]n)^{1/n}-n^{1/n}\right) \\
& = \lim_{n \to \infty}  \left([$a]^{1/n} \cdot n^{1/n} - n^{1/n}\right) \\
& = \lim_{n \to \infty} n^{1/n} \left([$a]^{1/n}-1\right)
\end{aligned}```]
From the two limits above, 
[``` \begin{aligned}
\lim_{n \to \infty} a_n & = \left(\lim_{n \to \infty} n^{1/n}\right)
\left(\lim_{n \to \infty} [$a]^{1/n} -1\right) \\
& = (1)(1-1) = 0
\end{aligned}```]
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
